From fabb2e2cb29469481dc069dda610a88610cf56b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 17:34:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] aunet/generate_bt: drive online bt generation through
 prefill (variable length)

Smoke on the real BPEByte 180k checkpoint crashed in forward_logits: the model's
training forward assumes the fixed training seq_len (position buffers / freqs_cis
sized to 8192), so it can't run on the variable-length sequences generation
produces. AU-Net's generator.prefill is the only variable-length forward, so
route generation through it instead.

- generate_bt.py: forward_fn now takes (token_rows, level_rows, row_ids) and
  returns per-row LAST-position logits (n_rows, V); online_bt_loop calls it with
  the active rows' variable-length lists. generate_online_bt takes the generator
  and packs active rows (concat tokens+levels, per-seq lengths) into one prefill
  call, reading logits at lengths.cumsum-1.
- hierarchical.py: drop the now-unused forward_logits (fixed-length only).
- eval.py: _generate_until_bt passes self.generator to generate_online_bt.
- test_generate_bt.py: forced forward updated to the new (rows, ids) signature.

Verified on GPU (consolidated bpebyte_br_bt_1.3B): generation runs end-to-end,
output is valid UTF-8, and committed patch boundaries match the offline
get_levels_mask of the generated bytes (subset + gap-free) with rollbacks firing.
All 6 CPU tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
